---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CTABanner from '../../components/CTABanner.astro';
import * as imgs from '../../data/images';
---

<Layout
  title="Fire-Rated Sealants | Simply Bespoke, North East England"
  description="Professional fire-rated sealant installation for commercial and residential buildings across the North East. Intumescent and fire-rated silicone sealant to specification."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container page-hero__content">
      <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--white">Commercial Service</span>
      <h1>Fire-Rated Sealants</h1>
      <p>Specialist fire-rated sealant application to joints, service penetrations and compartment boundaries in commercial and residential developments.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="fire-layout">
        <div class="fire-content">
          <span class="eyebrow">Fire Sealant Specialist</span>
          <h2>Fire-Rated Sealant Application</h2>
          <div class="prose">
            <p>Fire-rated sealants play a critical role in maintaining compartmentalisation in buildings — preventing the spread of fire and smoke through gaps, joints and service penetrations in fire-rated walls, floors and ceilings.</p>
            <p>Correct installation is essential. The sealant product must be appropriate for the specific joint configuration, substrates and fire resistance rating required. Simply Bespoke provides professional fire-rated sealant application to specification across the North East.</p>
            <h3>Fire Sealant Services</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Fire-rated joint sealing in walls and floors</li>
              <li>Service penetration sealing (pipes, cables, ducts)</li>
              <li>Linear gap sealing in fire compartment boundaries</li>
              <li>Intumescent sealant application</li>
              <li>Fire-rated silicone and mastic application</li>
              <li>Application to manufacturer and building regulation requirements</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Compliance</h3>
            <p>Fire-rated sealant installations must be carried out correctly and in accordance with the product manufacturer's instructions and relevant building regulations. We work to specification and use approved fire-rated sealant products appropriate to the specific application.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="btn-group">
            <a href="/contact" class="btn btn--primary">Discuss Your Requirements</a>
            <a href="/commercial" class="btn btn--outline">All Commercial Services</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="fire-aside">
          <div class="fire-callout">
            <h3>Important</h3>
            <p>Fire-rated sealant must be installed correctly to specification to be effective. Product selection, joint preparation and application method all affect performance.</p>
          </div>
          <img src={imgs.internal[5]} alt="Internal commercial sealant application" loading="lazy" class="fire-aside-img" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABanner
    title="Fire-Rated Sealant Across the North East"
    description="Professional fire-rated sealant installation for commercial and residential developments. Get in touch to discuss your project requirements."
    buttonText="Get in Touch"
  />
</Layout>

<style>
  .fire-layout {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 380px;
    gap: clamp(3rem,5vw,5rem); align-items: start;
  }
  .fire-aside { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem; position: sticky; top: 6rem; }
  .fire-callout {
    background: var(--color-navy); color: #fff;
    padding: 2rem; border-left: 4px solid var(--color-blue);
  }
  .fire-callout h3 { color: #fff; margin-bottom: .75rem; }
  .fire-callout p { color: rgba(255,255,255,.8); max-width: none; font-size: .9rem; }
  .fire-aside-img { aspect-ratio: 4/3; object-fit: cover; width: 100%; }

  @media (max-width: 1023px) {
    .fire-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .fire-aside { position: static; }
  }
</style>
